---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/ui/Tag.astro";

const stack = ["LLM Agent", "Text-to-SQL", "Python", "SQL", "Chart Rendering", "Telegram Bot API"];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="I Built a Chatbot That Found Our Hidden Money-Losing Products"
  description="A Telegram-based AI agent that lets non-technical teams query a live ERP database in plain language and get charts back instantly."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-28">
    <p class="label-mono mb-4">Case study</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight">I Built a Chatbot That Found Our Hidden Money-Losing Products</h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      One of my manager's businesses runs its operations on an ERP system that only the data/finance team could
      really query — everyone else waited on a report. I built a Telegram-based AI agent connected to that ERP
      database: ask a question in plain language, and it writes a safe, read-only SQL query, reasons about the
      result, and answers back with numbers and a chart in the same chat.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-6">
      {stack.map((t) => <Tag>{t}</Tag>)}
    </div>

    <!-- Video demo -->
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
      <video
        class="w-full h-auto block"
        poster="/video/agentic-erp-poster.jpg"
        controls
        preload="none"
        playsinline
      >
        <source src="/video/agentic-erp-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-2">
      Screen recording of the actual agent, live: from "which categories are most profitable" to spotting a hidden
      loss-maker to a revenue-vs-margin scatter plot — three questions, one conversation.
    </p>

    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-6">Business impact</p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-accent">Minutes</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Not days, to an answer</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-accent">Zero SQL</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Required from the asker</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-ink">No new tool</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Runs in existing chat</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-8 leading-relaxed">
      The video isn't a canned query — it's three real, follow-up questions in one conversation, the kind a
      commercial or finance lead actually asks once they see the first answer:
    </p>

    <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="12" width="5" height="9" />
            <rect x="9.5" y="7" width="5" height="14" />
            <rect x="16" y="3" width="5" height="18" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">See the full margin picture instantly.</span> Category-level gross
          profit and margin %, on demand — no waiting on finance to compile a report before a decision gets made.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-warn bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-warn-soft text-warn flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 3 2 20h20L12 3Z" />
            <line x1="12" y1="10" x2="12" y2="14.5" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="17.3" r="0.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Catch hidden loss-makers before they bleed further.</span> A follow-up
          question surfaces products that look like top sellers by revenue but carry thin or negative margin — the
          kind of problem that usually hides in a spreadsheet until quarter-end close.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="6" cy="17" r="2" />
            <circle cx="12.5" cy="8" r="2.4" />
            <circle cx="19" cy="13.5" r="1.7" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Turn the finding into a decision-ready visual.</span> One more question
          renders a revenue-vs-margin scatter plot, instantly separating stars, cash cows, and quiet loss-makers —
          ready to drop into a leadership deck, not just a raw table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-6">One chat, the whole ERP</p>

    <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
      The video above is just <span class="text-ink font-medium">one conversation</span> — gross profit by product.
      That's not the ceiling, it's one thread. The same agent is wired into every module the ERP has:
      <span class="text-ink font-medium">AR, AP, Sales, Purchasing, Logistics, Inventory</span> — all of it, answered
      in the same chat window.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-4">
      That matters because most ERP reports live behind an export button: open Excel, wait for forty columns to
      load, pivot a table, hope you didn't miss a filter — then explain it to whoever actually asked. A business
      owner doesn't have time for that between meetings, so the report waits, or someone else reads it for them.
      With this agent, <span class="text-ink font-medium">that whole step disappears.</span> Ask a question, in any
      module, and it reads the underlying report the way an analyst would — then hands back the answer, not the
      spreadsheet.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mt-6">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M4 13v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6" />
            <polyline points="8 9 12 13 16 9" />
            <line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="13" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Accounts Receivable</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"Who's overdue past 60 days?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M4 13v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6" />
            <polyline points="8 7 12 3 16 7" />
            <line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Accounts Payable</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"What do we owe suppliers this week?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="9" cy="20" r="1.3" />
            <circle cx="18" cy="20" r="1.3" />
            <path d="M2.5 3h2l2.6 12.2a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.6h8.6a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.6L21 7H6" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Sales</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"Which region is behind target?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="5.5" y="4" width="13" height="17" rx="2" />
            <rect x="9" y="2.3" width="6" height="3" rx="1" />
            <line x1="8.5" y1="10.5" x2="15.5" y2="10.5" />
            <line x1="8.5" y1="14.5" x2="15.5" y2="14.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Purchasing</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"Which POs are late from the supplier?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="2" y="8" width="11" height="8" rx="1" />
            <path d="M13 11h4l3.5 3v2H13z" />
            <circle cx="6.5" cy="18.3" r="1.6" />
            <circle cx="16.5" cy="18.3" r="1.6" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Logistics</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"Which shipments are delayed right now?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M21 8v8l-9 5-9-5V8l9-5 9 5Z" />
            <path d="M3 8l9 5 9-5" />
            <line x1="12" y1="13" x2="12" y2="21" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink text-sm">Inventory</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-xs mt-1 leading-snug">"Which SKUs are about to run out?"</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-ink-faint mb-2">Before</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Open the ERP, export to Excel, filter, pivot, cross-reference another sheet — then explain it to whoever
          actually asked.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-l-4 border-l-accent border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-accent mb-2">After</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Type the question into the same Telegram chat everyone already has open. Get the answer — and the chart
          — back in seconds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <details class="mt-16 group">
      <summary class="label-mono cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-open:rotate-90">›</span>
        How it works (technical)
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-6">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 200" class="w-full h-auto" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: user question flows through the LLM agent, which queries the ERP database read-only, then formats the result as a chart back to the user">
          <g class="stroke-ink-faint" stroke-width="2">
            <line x1="180" y1="100" x2="264" y2="100" />
            <line x1="470" y1="100" x2="554" y2="100" />
            <line x1="760" y1="100" x2="844" y2="100" />
          </g>
          <g class="fill-ink-faint">
            <polygon points="264,93 264,107 278,100" />
            <polygon points="554,93 554,107 568,100" />
            <polygon points="844,93 844,107 858,100" />
          </g>

          <!-- node 1: user -->
          <g>
            <rect x="20" y="60" width="160" height="80" rx="14" class="fill-surface stroke-border" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <circle cx="70" cy="100" r="18" class="fill-accent" opacity="0.85" />
            <text x="100" y="94" font-size="13" font-weight="600" class="fill-ink" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">You ask</text>
            <text x="100" y="112" font-size="11" class="fill-ink-muted" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">plain language</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node 2: LLM agent -->
          <g>
            <rect x="270" y="50" width="200" height="100" rx="14" class="fill-surface stroke-border" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <circle cx="330" cy="100" r="20" class="fill-accent" />
            <circle cx="330" cy="100" r="7" class="fill-surface" />
            <text x="365" y="94" font-size="13" font-weight="600" class="fill-ink" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">LLM agent</text>
            <text x="365" y="112" font-size="11" class="fill-ink-muted" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">writes SQL</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node 3: ERP DB -->
          <g>
            <ellipse cx="610" cy="72" rx="50" ry="16" class="fill-accent" opacity="0.85" />
            <rect x="560" y="72" width="100" height="56" class="fill-accent" opacity="0.75" />
            <ellipse cx="610" cy="128" rx="50" ry="16" class="fill-accent-strong" />
            <text x="610" y="165" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-ink-muted" font-family="ui-monospace, monospace">ERP DB (read-only)</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node 4: chart back -->
          <g>
            <rect x="850" y="50" width="150" height="100" rx="14" class="fill-surface stroke-border" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <rect x="875" y="105" width="14" height="25" class="fill-accent" opacity="0.5" />
            <rect x="898" y="90" width="14" height="40" class="fill-accent" opacity="0.75" />
            <rect x="921" y="75" width="14" height="55" class="fill-accent" />
            <text x="925" y="65" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-ink" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif">Answer</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          The agent only ever runs read-only, parameterized queries against a scoped set of views — it can't write,
          and it can't touch tables outside what it's been given access to. Every response is grounded in the actual
          query result, not a free-form guess, which is what makes it safe to hand to non-technical users.
        </p>
        <div class="text-ink-muted space-y-4 leading-relaxed mt-6 text-sm">
          <p>
            The hardest part wasn't generating SQL — it was generating <em>correct</em> SQL against a real ERP
            schema, where naive queries silently double-count. For example, the sales-invoice table is a rolling
            ledger, so a query that sums it directly across periods can overcount. The agent has to reason about
            snapshot periods and stated caveats, not just table joins, and explain that reasoning back to the user
            (visible in the video as the "Caveat" and "Scope" notes before the numbers).
          </p>
          <p>
            On the output side, the agent decides whether a question is best answered as a table, a single number,
            or a chart — and when it picks a chart, it renders one and sends the image back into the same chat
            thread, so the whole interaction stays in one place instead of bouncing the user out to a dashboard.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Data viz showcase -->
    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-6">Sample outputs</p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 items-start">
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <img src="/video/agentic-erp-table.jpg" alt="Gross profit by category table output from the agent" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <img src="/video/agentic-erp-chart.jpg" alt="Scatter plot from the agent showing revenue vs. gross margin, flagging hidden loss-making products" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
